"web\",\n   \"kind\": \"ui-detail\",\n   \"executor\": \"factory\",\n   \"complexity\": \"standard\",\n   \"items\": [\n    \"Back link; request title, area, priority badge, status badge, created date, and description or “No description.”\",\n    \"Show “Request not found.” and a link back to Requests for an unknown ID\",\n    \"Show Start work for Open, Mark done for In progress, and Reopen for Done\",\n    \"After a successful status change, show the new status badge and corresponding next action; on failure show “Could not update the request.” and retain the prior status badge\",\n    \"Status and priority badges use the specified colors and include readable text labels\",\n    \"Created date displayed without time or timezone, in a date-only format such as “8 Oct 2026”\",\n    \"Every control is keyboard reachable; text meets WCAG AA contrast\"\n   ],\n   \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"EST-3\",\n    \"EST-5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"EST-10\",\n   \"title\": \"Automated request business-rule test cases\",\n   \"feature\": \"F-5\",\n   \"track\": \"qa\",\n   \"kind\": \"qa-cases\",\n   \"executor\": \"factory\",\n   \"complexity\": \"standard\",\n   \"items\": [\n    \"Automated cases for valid creation with Open status; missing and too-short title rejection; missing area rejection; too-long description rejection\",\n    \"Automated cases for all three allowed status transitions and rejection of a disallowed transition\",\n    \"Automated cases for filtered newest-first listing and unknown-ID not-found behavior\"\n   ],\n   \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"EST-2\",\n    \"EST-3\",\n    \"EST-4\",\n    \"EST-5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"EST-11\",\n   \"title\": \"Automated list-to-completion end-to-end test\",\n   \"feature\": \"F-5\",\n   \"track\": \"qa\",\n   \"kind\": \"qa-e2e\",\n   \"executor\": \"factory\",\n   \"complexity\": \"standard\",\n   \"items\": [\n    \"Run the list, create, open, Start work, Mark done, and Done-filter workflow\",\n    \"Verify the created request appears at the top, then appears in the Done-filtered list after completion\"\n   ],\n   \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"EST-7\",\n    \"EST-8\",\n    \"EST-9\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"EST-12\",\n   \"title\": \"Client acceptance testing\",\n   \"feature\": \"F-5\",\n   \"track\": \"qa\",\n   \"kind\": \"qa-uat\",\n   \"executor\": \"human\",\n   \"complexity\": \"standard\",\n   \"items\": [\n    \"Client acceptance testing and regression pass\"\n   ],\n   \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"EST-10\",\n    \"EST-11\"\n   ],\n   \"overhead\": \"Client UAT is a required human acceptance activity and does not deliver a specification requirement.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"EST-13\",\n   \"title\": \"Client liaison and project management\",\n   \"feature\": \"F-5\",\n   \"track\": \"pm\",\n   \"kind\": \"pm-management\",\n   \"executor\": \"human\",\n   \"complexity\": \"standard\",\n   \"items\": [\n    \"Client liaison, scope decisions, and sign-offs\"\n   ],\n   \"dependsOn\": [],\n   \"overhead\": \"Required human client liaison and project-management overhead; factory planning and coordination of its own work are excluded.\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"requirements\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"ears\": \"The maintenance request system shall provide a browser-accessible web front end, an HTTP API, and a database that stores request records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"ears\": \"When an empty database is initialized, the maintenance request system shall seed exactly eight requests: four Open including exactly one Urgent, two In progress, and two Done, with every supported area represented.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"ears\": \"The maintenance request system shall persist request records across browser reloads and application restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"ears\": \"The API shall expose exactly four request operations and no others: list requests, create a request, get a request by ID, and change a request's status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a client lists requests, the API shall return all requests or only requests matching one requested status, ordered newest first.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a client creates a valid request, the maintenance request system shall assign an ID and UTC creation time and set its status to Open.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a client submits a request for creation, the maintenance request system shall require a title trimmed to 3 to 80 characters, an area of Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, or Reception, a priority of Low, Normal, or Urgent, and an optional description of at most 500 characters, rejecting invalid values with an error naming the field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"ears\": \"The API shall keep title, area, priority, and description fixed after creation and reject attempts to change those fields or delete a request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"ears\": \"The maintenance request API shall accept only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open status transitions, reject all other status changes, return a not-found response for a status change on an unknown request ID, and return an error without changing any request when the status-change body is missing or its status value is unrecognized.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Requests screen shall display the Hive Works wordmark, the signed-in demo user's initials SC, a status filter with All, Open, In progress, and Done choices with All selected initially, a New request button, and a newest-first request list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a user selects a status filter or returns from request detail, the Requests screen shall load the list for the selected filter and retain that filter on return from detail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the user opens New request, the Requests screen shall show a dialog with Title, Area, Priority defaulting to Normal, and Description fields, plus Create and Cancel controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"ears\": \"When valid request creation succeeds, the Requests screen shall close the dialog, select All, and show the new Open request at the top of the list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a create field fails validation, the Requests screen shall keep the dialog open and display the field's error message under that field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the create API call fails for a reason other than field validation, the Requests screen shall show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, retain entered values, and allow retry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n  \"ears\": \"While requests are loading, absent for the selected filter, or fail to load, the Requests screen shall display the corresponding loading, empty, or error state with retry available for load errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a request exists, the request detail screen shall display a back link, its title, area, priority badge, status badge, created date, and description or “No description.” when the description is empty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n  \"ears\": \"The request detail screen shall show Start work for Open, Mark done for In progress, and Reopen for Done.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a status change succeeds or fails, the request detail screen shall show the new status and corresponding action only after success, or show “Could not update the request.” while retaining the prior status after failure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a request ID does not exist, the request detail screen shall display “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n  \"ears\": \"The maintenance request screens shall use one light theme, one sans-serif font, a neutral background, near-black text, and the specified status and priority badge colors with text labels on every badge.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n  \"ears\": \"The maintenance request screens shall show request dates as date-only values, use stacked cards at 375 px and table rows at the fixed 1280 px viewport target, avoid horizontal page scrolling at those widths, label every field, and make every control keyboard reachable with WCAG AA text contrast.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n  \"ears\": \"The maintenance request system shall display created dates as date-only values such as “8 Oct 2026” without a time or timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-24\",\n  \"ears\": \"The maintenance request application shall include automated tests for the request business rules and an end-to-end list-to-completion workflow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"settings\" kind=\"settings\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"deliveryModel\": \"agentic\",\n \"stackSource\": \"undecided\",\n \"designInTotal\": true,\n \"feedbackRounds\": 2,\n \"noRepo\": true,\n \"client\": \"The ignite studio\",\n \"projectName\": \"Maintenance Request\",\n \"pm\": \"Ahsan Raza\",\n \"humanReview\": true,\n \"drawDesign\": false\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"known-stack\" kind=\"known-stack\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"repo\": false,\n \"stackChosenBy\": \"undecided\"\n}\n</artifact>\n\nSize the tasks (independent estimator 1 of 3)."}